INE présente Sous Influence, une nouvelle exposition réunissant dix artistes émergents dans un lieu bruxellois inédit de 1 000 m². À travers la peinture, la photographie, le textile, la sculpture et l’installation, l’exposition pose une question centrale : sommes-nous vraiment les auteurs de ce que nous devenons ? Images, croyances, héritages familiaux et culturels, technologies, environnement ou encore structures sociales : de multiples influences façonnent, consciemment ou non, notre manière de penser, d’agir et de nous définir. Sous Influence explore ces mécanismes parfois invisibles et la manière dont ils participent à la construction de notre identité et de notre rapport au monde. Les dix artistes réunis pour l’occasion abordent cette question depuis des perspectives et des expériences très différentes. Religion et spiritualité, omniprésence…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700027216","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700028075","title":"BAFF- Brussels Art Film Festival","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-n2973404428","start":"2026-11-09T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-15T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"BAFF 2026 : 25 ans de cinéma, d’art et de création Du 10 au 15 novembre 2026, le Brussels Art Film Festival (BAFF) célèbre sa 25e édition à Bruxelles, Anvers et Mons. Seul festival en Belgique consacré aux documentaires sur l’art et la création, il invite à explorer six jours durant les liens entre cinéma, musique, danse, littérature, poésie et arts plastiques. Au programme : 38 films, 13 films belges en compétition et une vingtaine de Premières belges, pour découvrir des artistes, des œuvres et des univers singuliers. De Marina Abramović à Germaine Acogny, de William S. Burroughs à Barbara Hammer, le festival fait dialoguer les pratiques, les époques et les regards. Pour cette édition anniversaire, le collage s’impose comme fil rouge : des fragments d’images, de récits et de mémoires s’assemblent, se confrontent et ouvrent de nouvelles perspectives. Une démarche qui traverse toute la…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":1.25,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/a00ae828a83bbee6be3841c6dc9fc6af3f115aff.png","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700028075","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bozar-central-never-alone","title":"Central. Never Alone","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n9329458664","start":"2026-11-10T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-01-24T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"The Brussels-based office Central (°2015) develops meaningful architecture that enhances the urban context and contributes to the public realm. For Central, the discipline of architecture is intrinsically relational — never autonomous, but always shaped by context and uses, collaborations and a frame of reference.From 11 November 2026 to 24 January 2027, Bozar and A+ present Never Alone. The exhibition starts from Central Office for Architecture and Urbanism’s first retrospective publication, bringing together an overview of both its completed and ongoing projects. The practice’s approach is…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://www.bozar.be/sites/default/files/styles/small_card_landscape_no_crop/public/media/images/False_904.jpg?itok=yDN_wuUh","sourceURL":"https://www.bozar.be/en/calendar/central-never-alone","sourceName":"Bozar","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"bxl-5700027001","title":"MAD Parcours 2026","category":"art","venueID":"v-47ce3802a20e","start":"2026-11-11T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-14T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Cette troisième édition rassemble une diversité de créateur·ice·s bruxellois·es dans des ateliers, boutiques, concept stores, galeries, showrooms et autres adresses emblématiques. Tout au long du parcours, les lieux participants proposent des rencontres avec les créateur·ice·s, des présentations de collections, des lancements, des démonstrations de savoir-faire, des installations, ainsi qu'une sélection de pièces et d'objets à (re)découvrir, et, selon les envies, à acquérir. L'occasion de pousser les portes de lieux parfois méconnus, d'échanger avec celleux qui façonnent la création bruxelloise et de découvrir des créations, collections et objets qui témoignent de la diversité des approches et des savoir-faire présents sur la scène bruxelloise. Pour guider les visiteur·euse·s, le MAD Parcours propose plusieurs itinéraires thématiques permettant d'explorer la ville selon ses affinités.…","people":[],"isFree":true,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/dfcc65152d2b6c91dc8987edbb97daa9fc7337d4.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700027001","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700027989","title":"Courts + Queer Mais Trash 2026 Film Festival","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-n14131529401","start":"2026-11-19T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-11-26T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Courts Mais Trash revient pour une nouvelle édition à Bruxelles ! Après les grands frasques de son 20e anniversaire l'an dernier, Courts Mais Trash revient du 20 au 26 novembre 2026 et s'associe une nouvelle fois à Queer Mais Trash pour une semaine dédiée au cinéma indépendant, underground, politique et décalé. Le festival investira à nouveau l'Espace Magh du 20 au 22 novembre, puis, du 24 au 26 novembre, Courts Mais Trash retrouvera son lieu historique, Les Riches-Claires, pour ses séances emblématiques. Pendant six jours, plus de 5 000 festivalier·ère·s sont attendu·e·s pour des projections, des séances scolaires, des soirées festives et des rencontres professionnelles. Plus de 100 films seront projetés et plus de 40 cinéastes viendront présenter leurs œuvres et échanger avec le public. Une nouvelle édition qui promet, une fois encore, de marquer la scène artistique bruxelloise. Un…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":null,"sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700027989","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"bxl-5700019291","title":"Shaping the Possible. Pierre Lallemand, designer","category":"art","venueID":"v-53afd6db05eb","start":"2026-11-19T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-07T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Le Design Museum Brussels présente une exposition inédite consacrée à Pierre Lallemand, architecte et designer de la scène belge contemporaine. À travers un parcours riche et documenté, les publics sont invités à découvrir plus de trente années de création à la croisée du design et de l’architecture. Dessins préparatoires, maquettes, prototypes, objets, mobiliers et pièces expérimentales jalonnent l’exposition et donnent à voir l’univers singulier d’un créateur pour qui chaque projet est une recherche en soi. Le parcours met en lumière une œuvre où la rigueur technique dialogue constamment avec la liberté formelle et une réflexion critique sur notre environnement construit. Formé à Bruxelles à la fin des années 1970, Pierre Lallemand développe très tôt une approche personnelle du projet, nourrie par l’expérimentation, le goût du détail et un rapport direct à la fabrication. La première…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":1.25,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/5adf19d91f9f7d4d2c0d0374104b500611fb7127.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700019291","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":1},{"id":"bxl-5700023745","title":"Festival Cinemamed 2026","category":"cinema","venueID":"osm-w1334658369","start":"2026-11-25T23:00:00Z","end":"2026-12-04T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Le festival Cinemamed (Festival cinéma méditerranéen de Bruxelles) est de retour du 26 novembre au 4 décembre au Cinéma Palace et au Cinéma Aventure pour une nouvelle édition immanquable! Quelques projections auront lieu aussi à l’Espace Magh, au Cinéma Galeries, à Bozar, au W:Halll, au RITCS et à la Cinematek ! C’est le rendez-vous de l’année pour découvrir une sélection de films de qualité reflétant les réalités sociales et culturelles de tout le bassin méditerranéen. Au programme de cette 26e édition : des documentaires percutants, des fictions inédites, des courts métrages, des avant-premières, des concerts et une multitude d’évènements qui font l’ambiance chaleureuse et conviviale du Cinemamed ! Depuis 1989, le Cinemamed promeut le vivre ensemble et met en avant des thématiques engagées. C’est aussi un forum de réflexion et de dialogue entre personnes et cultures. Venez rencontrer…","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":1.25,"imageURL":"https://agendabrussels2.imgix.net/22039f786b2c713be2f3270b0c275449af03aafa.jpg","sourceURL":"https://visit.brussels/fr/visiteurs/agenda/event-detail.5700023745","sourceName":"agenda.brussels","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":0},{"id":"kanal-no-show","title":"NO SHOW","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-01-17T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Can a museum entertain? On the site of Brussels’ first luna park, artist duo Deborah Bowmann, musician Maoupa Mazzocchetti and 20 Brussels artists pose this question with a hint of irony. Their response takes shape in NO SHOW, where art, light, sound and performance converge in a fully immersive experience across five rooms. Rooted in the playful spirit of artist-run initiatives and in the structures that support them, NO SHOW explores how artists sustain their practices in a world increasingly geared towards quick pleasures, scattered attention and high consumption.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v7r3IAA.jpg?crop=5526%2C2891%2C0%2C553&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/no-show","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-joelle-tuerlinckx","title":"Joëlle Tuerlinckx","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"For several years, Joëlle Tuerlinckx kept a close eye on the construction of Kanal. With a light show and an explosive symphony of sounds co-created with Christoph Fink, she puts you under hypnosis and introduces you to the underground part of both the museum and her work. In the empty space, stories about foundations slowly blend with other tales.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v901IAA.jpg?crop=8256%2C4320%2C0%2C592&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/joelle-tuerlinckx","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-manon-de-boer","title":"Manon de Boer","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Amidst the bustle of the new museum and the city, Manon de Boer’s sound installation Blindsight invites you to slow down. Together with choreographer Latifa Laâbissi and sound designer Laszlo Umbreit, de Boer animates the voices of artists who inspire them, from Chantal Akerman to Beyoncé.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/2026-01/share.jpg?crop=1200%2C628%2C0%2C1&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/manon-de-boer","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-joshua-serafin","title":"Joshua Serafin","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-03-28T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"Why do we continue searching for what has been lost? In Whispering Pleas of the eternal echoes, you are invited to join the search for Joshua Serafin’s roots. This immersive film installation weaves together scenes across countries and generations. In the artist’s unique cosmology, past and present enter into conversation.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v8FFIAY.jpg?crop=4672%2C2445%2C0%2C1799&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/joshua-serafin","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-otobong-nkanga","title":"Otobong Nkanga","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-18T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"For the opening of Kanal, Otobong Nkanga weaves stories through threads. An installation of looms becomes the backdrop for encounters and conversations about sustainability and ownership, but also about the museum’s role in the social ecosystem.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v8yPIAQ.jpg?crop=2975%2C1556%2C0%2C2334&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/otobong-nkanga","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-infinite-woman","title":"An infinite woman","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-04-25T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"A century ago, the mass-produced image of a Mangbetu woman went viral. An infinite woman explores how the distinctive profile of the Mangbetus from Congo became a modernist and colonial emblem after Citroën’s La Croisière Noire expedition, but also a powerful catalyst for artists. Through archives and works by contemporary artists like Carrie Mae Weems, Frida Orupabo and Magdalene Odundo, the exhibition celebrates the limitless Black female imagination in resisting the colonial algorithm.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003wE0rIAE.png?crop=1200%2C628%2C0%2C83&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/infinite-woman","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-banu-cennetoglu","title":"Banu Cennetoğlu","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-23T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"What do human rights mean today, in a world where they continue to be undermined and violated? In right?, Banu Cennetoğlu presents the articles of the Universal Declaration of Human Rights of 1948 in bouquets of gold letter balloons in Kanal’s showroom. As the balloons slowly deflate, the work questions the language of rights and the human rights framework the Declaration helped put into place. It reflects on what these rights mean, their history and lofty rhetoric, but also on how their inherent promises visibly fade.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003vXbpIAE.jpg?crop=5239%2C2741%2C0%2C2557&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/banu-cennetoglu","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-right-city-right-future","title":"Right to the City - Right to the Future","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-30T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"\"Brussels\" is blamed for everything. The city has become a symbol of dysfunction, bureaucracy and fragmentation. The exhibition Right to the city organised by Kanal Architecture presents a different view: a critical homage that positions Brussels as a pioneering laboratory for a new spatial practice. A practice that is based less on the linear logic of a masterplan than on conflictual, antagonistic and participatory processes that define, renegotiate and reinvent our ways of living together in the city.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/2026-01/share.jpg?crop=1200%2C628%2C0%2C1&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/right-city-right-future","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-departement-des-pieges","title":"Département des Pièges","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2027-05-30T21:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"With a wink to Brussels artist Marcel Broodthaers, Clémentine Deliss invites you to enter the Département des Pièges. Here, you will find a selection of unexpected artefacts and paintings from 11 Brussels museums, as well as works by contemporary artists. From elaborate fishnets to hunting decoys, psychiatric tests and trompe l’oeil paintings, each exhibit relates to the concept of the trap. You are invited to study these diverse traps and participate in this \"museum-university\".","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003v7cXIAQ.jpg?crop=7951%2C4161%2C0%2C569&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/departement-des-pieges","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2},{"id":"kanal-truly-immense-journey","title":"A truly immense journey","category":"art","venueID":"osm-n13514985008","start":"2026-11-27T23:00:00Z","end":"2028-01-09T22:59:00Z","openingNight":null,"summary":"A truly immense journey guides you through the forces that have set people, ideas and artistic forms in motion from the early 20th century to today. The exhibition spans modern icons such as Lygia Clark, Sonia Delaunay, Alberto Giacometti, Natalia Goncharova, Wifredo Lam and Henri Matisse, alongside contemporary international and Brussels-based artists including Sammy Baloji, Edith Dekyndt and Hana Miletić. More than 350 works, predominantly from the Centre Pompidou and Kanal, but also from numerous Belgian public and private holdings are brought together.","people":[],"isFree":false,"priceFrom":null,"imageURL":"https://kanal.b-cdn.net/sites/default/files/sparklink/a0wSm000003vXdWIAU.jpg?crop=6454%2C3377%2C0%2C2273&width=1200","sourceURL":"https://kanal.brussels/en/calendar/truly-immense-journey","sourceName":"Kanal–Centre Pompidou","isFestival":false,"showtimes":[],"soldOut":null,"fewLeft":null,"reviews":[],"selected":true,"spotNote":null,"artistPick":false,"goodPick":2}]}